GNU grep sources for Debian
---------------------------

GNU grep’s official distribution point is a CVS server, but the FSF
helpfully supplies a Git repository as well.  This Debian package is
developed in a public Git repository (see the Vcs-Git field of
debian/control) based on the repository at <git://git.sv.gnu.org/grep>.
To build from a git checkout:

	uscan
	debian/autogen.sh
	debuild -I -i

To build a released version, no special instructions apply.
“dpkg-buildpackage” and “apt-get -b grep” should work as usual.

